tar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T15:52:36-07:00","id":1263914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1263909#post1263909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have brief descriptions of the settings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cyberpunk vampires, space vampires, European monarchist vampires, apocalyptic vampires, alternate history noir vampires, Korean Empire vampires<br /> <br /> (having only skimmed at this point)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T15:58:02-07:00","id":1263915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1263909#post1263909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have brief descriptions of the settings?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Ascendency:</b> Futuristic megacity where cybernetics are outstripping magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Crown Games: </b>Europe is ruled by empowered Divine Right monarchs (empowered, specifically, by the Christian God). Because a not insignificant number of the nobility are now vampires, society and technology at large is relatively archaic.<br /> <br /> <b>The End of the World: </b>What it says on the tin; but it was caused by a bio-weapon that makes feeding... dangerous. Default setting is Singapore.<br /> <br /> <b>Night Without End: </b>Vampires in SPAAAAACE.<br /> <br /> <b>Rain Falls: </b>Hard-boiled vampires. Noire aesthetic<sup>TM</sup> above all.<br /> <br /> <b>War Drums: </b>Tail end of 16<sup>th</sup> Century China, Japan, and Korea, with Korea being invaded by Japan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T16:41:06-07:00","id":1263929,"title":"","content":"Crown Games allows for any real political stage, the sample Chronicle is 'Dragons in the House of Romanov,' featuring the Russian Empire in 2018.<br /> <br /> I don't know if any writers or the developer are here but the coteries section is great, I really like the inclusion of colonies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-31-2018, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T16:46:58-07:00","id":1263931,"title":"","content":"Yeah they seem interesting, Coteries always seemed odd to me given Vamps themes compared to the groups in other splats and that now as more books are being released they get no mechanical benefit so these seem cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T18:25:40-07:00","id":1263945,"title":"","content":"Am I missing something or does the &quot;Colony of Bats&quot; subsection never <i>actually </i>explain how Colonies form, other than that they're an extension of the related phenomena of Feeding Grounds, Havens, and Herds? I do appreciate the irony that thoroughly socially and metaphysically bonded Kindred groups are seen as a blight upon vampires as a whole, but it feels like I'm missing something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 10-31-2018, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T18:50:25-07:00","id":1263950,"title":"","content":"Guide to the Night is very <i>&quot;meh!&quot;</i> so far (I actually read the whole thing now, I was not impressed with what I saw).<br /> <br /> It wasted a large number of pages on alternative settings for vampires. Not something I wanted. I'd rather they expanded on the core Vampire the Requiem setting, instead of adding Vampirehammer 40k, Fallout: The Requiem, Dungeons &amp; Vampires, Cybervampire 2020, etc. (not the actual titles of these side settings, but you get the point, it's basically pretty out there and 100% unrelated to the core Vampire the Requiem setting).<br /> On top of that, they added social combat, Lingua Bellum, which is cool, but it got too much page count dedicated to something that only has niche applications (the book straight up admits that Lingua Bellum will find little use in games outside of grand debates in Elysiums). They went pretty overboard on the mechanics (making it as complex as physical combat) and made it more complicated than necessary, wasting a lot of pages on something that will likely be used very sparsely in an average Vampire chronicle.<br /> The book also comes with advice for players and storytellers, but most of the advice is pretty obvious stuff that I think most storytellers were already doing before Guide of the Night (even one of my friends, who is a newbie storyteller, is already doing most of the things mentioned in Guide of the Night). I personally got nothing new out of it, but I can see it being useful for players who want to become first-time storytellers but feel intimidated by the idea of taking on that responsibility.<br /> The majority of the new Merits, Devotions and Conditions are tied to the earlier mentioned side settings and not readily usable in a regular Vampire the Requiem game (who's ever gonna use space travel Merits/Conditions/Devotions in a normal Requiem game? Like, seriously?), which is also a damn shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 11-01-2018, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T19:15:23-07:00","id":1263952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1263945#post1263945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing something or does the &amp;quot;Colony of Bats&amp;quot; subsection never <i>actually </i>explain how Colonies form, other than that they're an extension of the related phenomena of Feeding Grounds, Havens, and Herds? I do appreciate the irony that thoroughly socially and metaphysically bonded Kindred groups are seen as a blight upon vampires as a whole, but it feels like I'm missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should we put that on Errata?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T02:26:50-07:00","id":1263996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1263950#post1263950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guide to the Night is very <i>&quot;meh!&quot;</i> so far (I only skimmed it but I was not impressed with what I saw).<br /> <br /> It wasted a large number of pages on alternative settings for vampires. Not something I wanted. I'd rather they expanded on the core Vampire the Requiem setting, instead of adding Vampirehammer 40k, Fallout: The Requiem, Dungeons &amp; Vampires, Cybervampire 2020, etc. (not the actual titles of these side settings, but you get the point, it's basically pretty out there and 100% unrelated to the core Vampire the Requiem setting).<br /> On top of that, they added social combat, Lingua Bellum, which is cool, but it got too much page count dedicated to something that only has niche applications (the book straight up admits that Lingua Bellum will find little use in games outside of grand debates in Elysiums). They went pretty overboard on the mechanics (making it as complex as physical combat) and made it more complicated than necessary, wasting a lot of pages on something that will likely be used very sparsely in an average Vampire chronicle.<br /> The book also comes with advice for players and storytellers, but most of the advice is pretty obvious stuff that I think most storytellers were already doing before Guide of the Night (even one of my friends, who is a newbie storyteller, is already doing most of the things mentioned in Guide of the Night). I personally got nothing new out of it, but I can see it being useful for players who want to become first-time storytellers but feel intimidated by the idea of taking on that responsibility.<br /> The majority of the new Merits, Devotions and Conditions are tied to the earlier mentioned side settings and not readily usable in a regular Vampire the Requiem game (who's ever gonna use space travel Merits/Conditions/Devotions in a normal Requiem game? Like, seriously?), which is also a damn shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately I must agree with you on almost everything. I don't like the turn requiem is taking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I bought it on trust but if I could go back I'd not have bought it. Just a couple of nice devotions. No more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-01-2018, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T05:38:43-07:00","id":1264013,"title":"","content":"I tend to incorporate a lot of weirdness into my games, so those alternate settings have actually put it higher on my list of ones to pick up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T09:51:59-07:00","id":1264063,"title":"","content":"High weirdness is fun to play around with. I\u2019m usually very adverse to alternate settings. But these ones were presented more in the demon style of shards which was really a nice change of pace. Since I just don\u2019t care for city settings. <br /> <br /> I think one of the best aspects of the book, is even if I don\u2019t use the ideas as presented. It is full of inspirational material. That would be fun to include in my current game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24316-mrowl","name":"MrOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T11:57:31-07:00","id":1264091,"title":"","content":"Any RPG supplement that makes reference to the Gish Gallup is aces in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T12:19:14-07:00","id":1264097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1263950#post1263950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I only skimmed it)</div> </div> </div> </div>...aaaaaand come back when you've read through the whole thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T12:49:38-07:00","id":1264101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264097#post1264097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...aaaaaand come back when you've read through the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...oooooookay, well, here I am, I'm back, and I read the whole thing.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry to say but my opinion hasn't really changed, though I'm a bit less pessimistic about Lingua Bellum than I originally was, and there are a few sparse hidden gems hidden in the Chapter 5. I also liked the material written on building cohesive player coteries. Most of the information and advice in Guide to the Night is extremely basic and bare bones though, with very obvious examples and suggestion that even my newbie Storyteller friend already figured out after Storytelling 3 to 4 sessions. The provided plot hooks... well, some were pretty interesting, while others once again seemed rather clich\u00e9 and basic.<br /> There are also other things in the book that I really don't like, such as the absolute preachy and infantile 'keeping the table safe' part, which I don't want to further get into.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm sorry, but my opinion stays the same, this book is clearly not for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 11-01-2018, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T14:02:18-07:00","id":1264112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264101#post1264101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than that, I'm sorry, but my opinion stays the same, this book is clearly not for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point being, don't make declarative statements about a work if all you've done is skimmed it and not see everything in context.<br /> <br /> But now you have. And if you don't like the product, ok then.<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are also other things in the book that I really don't like, such as the absolute preachy and infantile 'keeping the table safe' part, which I don't want to further get into. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://awesomelytechie.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/Head-desk.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ...really? Are we really going to do this again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T14:30:20-07:00","id":1264116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264112#post1264112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...really? Are we really going to do this again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember the lessons of Cam/Paulie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T14:34:18-07:00","id":1264118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264116#post1264116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the lessons of Cam/Paulie.</div> </div> </div> </div>...who dat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T14:34:37-07:00","id":1264119,"title":"","content":"So I gotta chime in. That guide to the night is both a storyteller and player book. And greet. As storytellers we definitely benefit from utizing A lot of the intro already. But not every player has that sort of instinct necessary to really drive home a great game and character. But guide to the night is a very gentle approach to passionately portraying your pc. And if your storyteller has the info down. Awesome. But for anyone at any table for any game really that wants to get the most out of the expirence for themselves and others. Guide to the night is a welcome treasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24316-mrowl","name":"MrOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T15:02:42-07:00","id":1264129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264118#post1264118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...who dat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, were you not there for that debacle? Paulie Romanov, now on the forums as Camilla, one of those &quot;bring pet peeves into every conversation&quot; types? Gecko might be a better comparison if you weren't there.<br /> <br /> Though I do have to say...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also other things in the book that I really don't like, such as the absolute preachy and infantile 'keeping the table safe' part, which I don't want to further get into.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you don't like it, that's one thing, but if we want to talk about infantile, the attitude I remember on the playground looks a lot more like yours than safe table practices.<br /> <br /> There's nothing childish about taking care of the people at your table, and if in fact you think RPG's should be an open place to just do whatever regardless of how that affects people, you end up looking more like the schoolyard bully who thinks they're too cool for human decency but are basically just that asshole everyone hates rather than, you know, an actually edgy and transgressive cool dude.<br /> <br /> No one likes a try-hard goth-punk poser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T15:33:14-07:00","id":1264142,"title":"","content":"Like, seriously, I get if someone doesn't feel like their table needs it, and if that trust exists, that's cool, and in that way I can understand the &quot;preachy&quot; argument even if I disagree with it, but seriously, infantile?<br /> <br /> Wut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T15:42:58-07:00","id":1264145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264129#post1264129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, were you not there for that debacle? Paulie Romanov, now on the forums as Camilla, one of those &quot;bring pet peeves into every conversation&quot; types? Gecko might be a better comparison if you weren't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh THAT Cam.<br /> <br /> I had no idea their other name was Paulie, so that didn't immediately ring a bell. Otherwise, yeah I've caught a bit on that &quot;debacle&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T17:42:42-07:00","id":1264162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264112#post1264112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point being, don't make declarative statements about a work if all you've done is skimmed it and not see everything in context.<br /> <br /> But now you have. And if you don't like the product, ok then.<br /> <br /> However...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm allowed to give my opinion whenever I want. And trust me when I say that if I skim something, I make sure that I understand the context of what I'm reading. The reason I even mentioned it at all is for transparency sake. That way you can see &quot;hey, that guy is giving his opinion, but he only skimmed it, so I'm gonna take his word with a grain of salt.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264112#post1264112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...really? Are we really going to do this again?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we aren't going to do this again. I literally said I didn't want to get into it further. Did you read my comment at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 11-01-2018, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T17:57:05-07:00","id":1264164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264162#post1264162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, we aren't going to do this again. I literally said I didn't want to get into it further. Did you read my comment at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The sensible thing to do if you don't want to get into something is to not make a barely-concealed attempt at still getting into it and then complain when people call you on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T18:03:44-07:00","id":1264166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264162#post1264162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm allowed to give my opinion whenever I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But you aren't allowed to complain either if you choose to share that opinion in a public space and someone decides to critique it.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, we aren't going to do this again. I literally said I didn't want to get into it further. Did you read my comment at all? </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1264164#post1264164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sensible thing to do if you don't want to get into something is to not make a barely-concealed attempt at still getting into it and then complain when people call you on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Satchel said. If you didn't want to go into it again, why did you bother bringing it up at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T18:23:20-07:00","id":1264170,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Time to find something else on topic to talk about, thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T20:12:27-07:00","id":1264551,"title":"","content":"Not to sound flip or anything: this is basically like Danse Macabre but for 2e, right? That's what the description leads me to expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T08:35:33-08:00","id":1264742,"title":"","content":"So how good does Lingua Bellium functions. Does it tend to overcomplicate or does it has some fun things to add?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T08:43:21-08:00","id":1264743,"title":"","content":"At first i was on the &quot;meh&quot; side, but the more i read it the more i've grown to like it, most of the stuff is very usefeull for st beginners, but i really like some of the new devotions, the colonies mechanics, more information about how coteries interact with the all-night society and the alternate setting can provide interesting ideas, i would have loved to see more coils of the dragon, Theban and cru\u00e0c rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T11:38:47-08:00","id":1264764,"title":"","content":"The Bend Space Devotion for the Night Without End scenario lets you <i>teleport </i>for 2 Vitae. Now I want to make a Nightcrawler vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T07:11:41-08:00","id":1264957,"title":"","content":"After reading the book for myself I've been able to formulate an opinion. The Advice for STs and Players is very basic but could be helpful for people who are genuinely new to the game and are looking for ideas.<br /> <br /> The sample characters tend to be a bit basic (Oh look another Authoritarian Ventrue!) but that's fine as an example. The sample settings don't do a single thing for me. If I want a post apocalyptic game I've got Fallout, If I want the Grim Darkness of the far future there's 40k ect.<br /> <br /> The Social Combat mechanics honestly seem over designed. In a big way. The Coterie section actually seemed pretty solid.<br /> <br /> There was a bit on sexism being bad in the Noir section that I thought wasn't really needed. I'm pretty sure everyone knows sexism is bad and playing in a more historical time period means things like that are probably going to crop up. I've got faith that most groups, even new ones would hash all that out either before starting or during play without a reminder. Same feeling for the more generalized advice later in the book.<br /> <br /> I've always been of the opinion that if something really truly does bother you you should bring it up to the ST at the end of the scene or the end of the session.<br /> <br /> To sum it up this book isn't really my cup of tea though I can see why some people would enjoy it or find it very useful.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24063-admiral-cheesecake","name":"Admiral Cheesecake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T10:31:12-08:00","id":1266732,"title":"","content":"I'm torn... I want a new VTR book. Some of the settings (cyber vamps, medieval? vamps, noir vamps) sound interesting. Others sound interesting but very unlikely to help with any games I might play or run. But if the general advice is pretty basic, and there's a lot of stuff that's obvious and/or in other books, is there enough useful page count to be worth the $20? I'm torn, as the last books, while interesting, were also not as directly useful as I hoped.<br /> <br /> How much detail do the coteries thing and the colonies thing get? Those sound potentially pretty useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10328-bkwrm79","name":"bkwrm79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T05:11:15-08:00","id":1271098,"title":"","content":"Did I miss the &quot;Tier 3&quot; advice in this book, or did they drop it when the project changed hands?<br /> <br /> Not mad, but genuinely wanting to know if I missed it the page/chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T14:35:47-08:00","id":1272044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bkwrm79</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1266732#post1266732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm torn... I want a new VTR book. Some of the settings (cyber vamps, medieval? vamps, noir vamps) sound interesting. Others sound interesting but very unlikely to help with any games I might play or run. But if the general advice is pretty basic, and there's a lot of stuff that's obvious and/or in other books, is there enough useful page count to be worth the $20? I'm torn, as the last books, while interesting, were also not as directly useful as I hoped.<br /> <br /> How much detail do the coteries thing and the colonies thing get? Those sound potentially pretty useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought coteries/colonies got a pretty good word count. There is advice on creating coteries with deeper backgrounds, as well as NPC coteries and how to use them. <br /> <br /> There is also some cool advice on creating some novel mechanics to emphasize different themes of the game. The book makes explicit some clan/covenant specific themes and gives advice on city creation. <br /> <br /> I kind of felt like the alt-settings got too much space. I was hoping there would be a bit of expansion of the default setting. I also was sad that the tier content seemed to have been cut. <br /> <br /> Side note -- (and I super don't want to start an art argument) the art looks great. I've really been loving everything since A Thousand Years of Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T18:24:11-08:00","id":1272503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1271098#post1271098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss the &quot;Tier 3&quot; advice in this book, or did they drop it when the project changed hands?<br /> <br /> Not mad, but genuinely wanting to know if I missed it the page/chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just flat isn't in the book. No explanation has been given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T19:28:01-08:00","id":1272514,"title":"","content":"When I read the ToC I was like nope, not for me. From the reviews here I see I choose right. Hey, they tried something and it didn't work out, it happens to us all. <br /> <br /> I'm still looking forward to spilled blood, but after seeing the reviews of this book, I think they should really rethink Broken Mirror (or whatever it was called), that vampire shards book as I don't see it being popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T19:29:06-08:00","id":1272515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1272503#post1272503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just flat isn't in the book. No explanation has been given.</div> </div> </div> </div> The tier 3 part was the one interesting part I'd heard about ironically, it was the one part I was looking forward to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T00:28:01-08:00","id":1273679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1272514#post1272514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I read the ToC I was like nope, not for me. From the reviews here I see I choose right. Hey, they tried something and it didn't work out, it happens to us all.<br /> <br /> I'm still looking forward to spilled blood, but after seeing the reviews of this book, I think they should really rethink Broken Mirror (or whatever it was called), that vampire shards book as I don't see it being popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the settings in the book are not detailed enough to be shards. What annoys me is that the 'shard seeds' eat up a lot of the book, to the point there is very little info on how to guide stories in the vein of Vampires in Requiem. In short, I feel the book is not a 'Guide to the Night'.<br /> <br /> Broken Mirror on the other hand, is a dedicated shard book, focusing on a single change to the setting (albeit, I expect some variations within in regards to the 'hows and whys') so I imagine it won't suffer from the diffusion of trying to fit a wide variety of content. Which I think contributed in how Guide is perceived as less than what we hoped for.<br /> <br /> After all it is not like the content is bad, per say. It is not what we were expecting or as widely applicable as we hoped for, certainly. It is not a players guide and does not feel (but can function as) a storyteller's guide...<br /> It just feels anemic, like there was a disagreement behind the scenes and compromised were made. It is a shame, because the different sections of the book have potential if they were expanded upon. It is almost like they tried to write half of two separate books...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T00:54:29-08:00","id":1273684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1263835-guide-to-the-night-live-on-drpg?p=1273679#post1273679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all it is not like the content is bad, per say. It is not what we were expecting or as widely applicable as we hoped for, certainly.</div> </div> </div> </div>...which if I recall, is the sentiment people are feeling right now about the entire VtR2e gameline direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T01:20:54-08:00","id":1273686,"title":"","content":"They did change developers and were in the middle of a few books at the time...It might take until all the projects that changes hands' are released for them to reach solid ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}